  "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{1}(\\sqrt{3})$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $\\sqrt{3}$'s on the leading diagonal.\n\n- ${J}_{3}(5)$ represents a $3\\times 3$ Jordan block with $5$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(\\sqrt{3})=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{3}(5)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(\\sqrt{3})\\,\u2295\\,{J}_{3}(5)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
